{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.carrier_shape_gives_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.carrier_shape_gives_four","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L236-L242","doc":"**Not vacuous**: the carrier's own shape. `u = v = -2` on the all-`σ⁻¹` branch, blocks\n`[(x,-1),(x,-1)]` then `[(y,-1),(y,-1)]`, and the coefficient comes out `4` — matching\n`carrierChain` in the sibling file, whose `Δ = 2` then divides it. Recorded so the\ntheorem above cannot be read as holding because the coefficient is always zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.eps_eq_of_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.eps_eq_of_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L220-L234","doc":"**`ChainTriple.eps_eq`, derived.** Given the block structure and the two signed sums\nequalling the linking numbers, the hub longitude's degree-2 Magnus coefficient is\n`u * v` — which is precisely the hypothesis\n`ChainTripleMilnorVanishesByGcdDividesProduct.ChainTriple.eps_eq`, and with it the\n`gcd u v ∣ u * v` closure of route 3's chain residual goes through.\n\nThe hypotheses are the measured braid-word facts, named so that what is borrowed is\nvisible: `hA`/`hB` say the far components occupy disjoint ordered blocks, and `hsum`\nsays each block's signed sum is that pair's linking number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.underSum_eq_linking","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.underSum_eq_linking","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L210-L218","doc":"**The other half.** A run of `2 m` crossings between two strands alternates which\npasses under, so the hub records exactly `m` of them, every one carrying the run's sign\n`s`. Its signed contribution is therefore `m * s` — and the pair's total signed crossing\ncount is `2 * lk` by the definition of the linking number. The two agree.\n\nStated without division, as the identity it is: the *measured* inputs are that the run\nhas even length and that its length is `2|lk|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsCoeff_append_of_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsCoeff_append_of_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L191-L208","doc":"**The arithmetic core.** When the two far components occupy disjoint, ordered blocks\nof the hub's longitude — no `y` in the first, no `x` in the second — the degree-2 Magnus\ncoefficient is exactly the product of the blocks' signed sums, and the reverse ordering\nvanishes.\n\nThis is where the `u * v` of `ChainTriple.eps_eq` comes from. It is a fact about lists;\nno topology enters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsAux_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsAux_append","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L167-L189","doc":"Running the accumulator through a concatenation: the second block starts with\nwhatever `p`-signs the first block contributed.\n\n`p ≠ q` is needed and is not a technicality: a letter cannot be both the thing being\ncounted and the thing being counted *against*, and the chain triples this is applied to\nhave distinct components by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsAux_eq_of_no_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsAux_eq_of_no_p","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L153-L165","doc":"A block with no `p`-letters cannot grow the accumulator, so every `q`-letter is\nweighted by the *same* running total: the block contributes `s` times its own signed\nsum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsAux_eq_zero_of_no_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsAux_eq_zero_of_no_q","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L140-L151","doc":"A block with no `q`-letters contributes nothing: there is no `q` for a `p` to\nprecede. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsCoeff","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L137-L138","doc":"`ε_{p,q}(w)` — the coefficient of `h_p h_q` in the Magnus expansion of `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsAux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.epsAux","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L126-L135","doc":"The degree-2 Magnus coefficient, with the running total of `p`-signs carried\nexplicitly. `epsAux w p q s` is the signed count of `(p before q)` pairs in `w`, given\nthat `s` worth of `p`-signs has already been seen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.signSum_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.signSum_cons","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L121-L124","doc":"Peeling one letter off a signed sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.signSum_eq_zero_of_absent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.signSum_eq_zero_of_absent","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L111-L119","doc":"Signed sum of a block containing no `c`-letters is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.signSum_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.signSum_append","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L105-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.signSum_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.signSum_nil","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.signSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.signSum","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L99-L101","doc":"Signed sum of the letters belonging to component `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.Letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.EpsEqFromMonotonicity.Letter","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/EpsEqFromMonotonicity.lean#L96-L97","doc":"A letter of a longitude word: whose meridian it is, and the crossing's sign. ","signatureChunk":0}]}